{"summary":"The southern fiscal or fiscal shrike (Lanius collaris) is a member of the shrike family found through most of Sub-Saharan Africa. It is also sometimes named jackie hangman or butcher bird due to its habit of impaling its prey on acacia thorns to store the food for later consumption. It was previously lumped together with the northern fiscal (Lanius humeralis). Together they were known as the common fiscal.","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lanius collaris","cells":[[-21.6,16.5,1],[-21.0,14.4,1],[-17.0,12.3,1],[-21.6,15.8,2],[-19.0,13.0,1],[-19.6,13.7,1],[-21.0,16.5,1],[-19.0,14.4,1],[-20.3,13.7,1],[-19.6,15.8,1],[-17.0,13.0,1],[-21.0,15.1,2],[-20.3,14.4,1],[-21.6,15.1,2],[-19.0,15.1,1],[-19.0,15.8,2],[-19.6,14.4,1],[-19.0,16.5,2],[-21.0,30.6,1],[-18.3,32.0,1],[-19.0,32.7,1],[-21.0,25.0,1],[-19.6,31.3,1],[-18.3,31.3,1],[-20.3,28.5,1],[-18.3,32.7,2],[-17.6,31.3,2],[-20.3,32.7,1],[-19.6,32.7,2],[-20.3,31.3,1],[-20.3,30.6,1],[-19.6,29.2,1],[-22.9,17.2,1],[-24.8,20.0,1],[-21.6,16.5,1],[-24.8,16.5,1],[-30.4,20.0,1],[-28.6,18.6,1],[-26.7,17.2,1],[-31.7,20.0,1],[-33.4,20.7,1],[-34.0,17.9,2],[-24.8,15.1,2],[-25.5,16.5,1],[-26.1,15.8,1],[-26.7,17.9,1],[-32.8,20.7,1],[-23.6,14.4,1],[-22.9,16.5,1],[-34.6,22.1,1],[-29.2,18.6,1],[-27.4,18.6,1],[-22.9,15.1,1],[-28.6,21.4,1],[-22.9,17.9,1],[-28.0,16.5,1],[-21.6,15.8,1],[-27.4,17.9,1],[-24.8,22.1,1],[-32.8,20.0,2],[-32.8,22.1,1],[-25.5,15.8,1],[-31.7,17.9,1],[-24.8,17.9,1],[-28.6,17.9,1],[-32.2,20.7,1],[-22.3,15.1,2],[-23.6,15.1,2],[-27.4,22.1,2],[-32.2,20.0,2],[-28.6,16.5,1],[-29.8,17.2,1],[-23.6,16.5,1],[-24.2,17.9,1],[-28.6,17.2,1],[-26.1,20.0,2],[-24.8,15.8,2],[-29.2,19.3,2],[-23.6,17.2,1],[-27.4,17.2,1],[-26.7,15.1,1],[-23.6,15.8,2],[-24.2,16.5,2],[-22.9,15.8,2],[-26.7,16.5,2],[-31.7,19.3,2],[-26.7,22.1,1],[-29.2,17.9,1],[-28.6,20.0,2],[-25.5,20.7,2],[-31.7,18.6,2],[-34.6,21.4,2],[-31.1,22.1,1],[-28.6,20.7,2],[-26.7,20.7,2],[-26.1,20.7,2],[-31.1,19.3,2],[-33.4,20.0,3],[-30.4,17.9,2],[-28.0,17.2,2],[-32.2,18.6,2